  "evidencia": "Page: Gisken Armand. Sentence: Gisken Armand Lillo-Stenberg (born 26 November 1962) is a Norwegian actress.\nPage: Gisken Armand. Sentence: There she has performed in plays such as Henrik Ibsen's \"A Doll's House\" and Anton Chekhov's \"Three Sisters\".\nPage: A Doll's House. Sentence: A Doll's House (Bokmål: \"Et dukkehjem\" ; also translated as \"A Doll House\") is a three-act play written by Henrik Ibsen.\nPage: A Doll's House. Sentence: The play is set in a Norwegian town circa 1879.\nPage: Frøydis Armand. Sentence: She is the daughter of actor Eilif Armand, and sister of Merete Armand and Gisken Armand, both actresses.\nPage: A Commuter Kind of Love. Sentence: A Commuter Kind of Love (Norwegian: \"Kjærleikens ferjereiser\" ) is a 1979 Norwegian drama film directed by Hans Otto Nicolayssen, starring Eilif Armand, Frøydis Armand and Per Jansen.",
