        "original_id": "88f28204-cc09-59a5-af0c-743a87458e12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gisken Armand, Frøydis Armand, Eilif Armand, Merete Armand, Henrik Ibsen, Anton Chekhov, Hans Otto Nicolayssen, Per Jansen\n- Works: A Doll's House, Three Sisters, A Commuter Kind of Love\n- Topics: Norwegian theatre, family relationships\n\nFacts:\n- A Doll's House is a three-act play written by Henrik Ibsen.\n- A Doll's House is set in a Norwegian town circa 1879.\n- A Commuter Kind of Love is a 1979 Norwegian drama film directed by Hans Otto Nicolayssen and starring Eilif Armand, Frøydis Armand, and Per Jansen.\n- Gisken Armand Lillo-Stenberg was born on 26 November 1962 and is a Norwegian actress.\n- Frøydis Armand is the daughter of actor Eilif Armand and the sister of actresses Merete Armand and Gisken Armand.\n- Gisken Armand has performed in plays such as Henrik Ibsen's A Doll's House and Anton Chekhov's Three Sisters.",
